file_merger: percent-encoding applies to the partition value, not the column name (checkpoint 3)

Sentence: "Apply percent-encoding of UTF-8 bytes for characters outside `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`;
space → `%20`; `/` encoded as `%2F`", a sub-bullet of the `<col1>=<val1>/...` segment line. It
names no half. Every checkpoint-3 column name is inside the safe set, so the two readings are
byte-identical until checkpoint 4, where a field path such as `attrs["region"]` is a partition
column. Test correct_partition_nested/partition_by_map_value expects the directory
`attrs["region"]=east`; the reference's encode_partition_value is applied to the value only.
Three runs registered the question and all chose both halves and failed: min12-ABDJKMN on v0
(T44, Risk 15), min11-ABDFJKMN's first run (T47, Risk 20), min12-ABDJKMN on v4 (T46, Risk 10,
"encoding of the name half is untested in all likelihood"). Two runs never registered it,
encoded the value only, and passed (min11 repeat, min12 on v3).

--- a/file_merger/checkpoint_3.md
+++ b/file_merger/checkpoint_3.md
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
 - Emit directory tree inside `--output` using Hive-style segments:
   `<col1>=<val1>/<col2>=<val2>/.../`
   - Values derived after casting to resolved schema types
-  - Apply percent-encoding of UTF-8 bytes for characters outside `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`; space → `%20`; `/` encoded as `%2F`
+  - Values use percent-encoding of UTF-8 bytes for characters outside `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`; space → `%20`; `/` encoded as `%2F`
   - Null (missing) partition values use literal `_null`
 - Within each partition directory, write CSV files named sequentially:
   `part-00000.csv`, `part-00001.csv`, … (zero-padded width 5)
